}, {"w": "invaded", "s": 39.171, "e": 39.719}, {"w": "Sparta.", "s": 39.719, "e": 40.369}], "sentences": [{"text": "Did you know the Spartans delivered the greatest one-word threat in military history?", "s": 0.05, "e": 5.423}, {"text": "When King Philip the Second of Macedon, Alexander the Great's father, was conquering Greece, he sent a message to Sparta warning them: \"If I invade Laconia, I will turn you out, never to rise again.\"", "s": 5.603, "e": 19.696}, {"text": "Sparta was outnumbered, outgunned, and surrounded.", "s": 19.816, "e": 23.074}, {"text": "Instead of surrendering or begging for peace, the Spartan leaders sent back a single word on their reply tablet: \"If.\"", "s": 23.194, "e": 31.476}, {"text": "Philip got the message.", "s": 31.596, "e": 33.129}, {"text": "Despite conquering almost all of Greece, neither Philip nor Alexander the Great ever invaded Sparta.", "s": 33.249, "e": 40.369}]}